 a worker's labor for a hundred dollars  then that's what their labor is worth  when the capitalist only pays them fifty  dollars and then charges a hundred  so pays them only fifty dollars for  their labor but charges 100 for the  product to make a profit on the sale  they're stealing 50 from the worker and  as competition increases the  exploitation will only worsen monopolies  will appear and prices will rise which  while rate wages decrease  this will create more working poor and  even fewer jobs wealth will concentrate  in fewer and fewer people while the poor  will just get poorer and poorer and  poorer  and eventually the workers will snap and  revolt  this revolt will lead to communism in  fairly short order mark says first the  workers will take control of the  government and purge capitalism from the  system making the government socialist  it will take over the production of  goods and all industry  but the structure of that government  will eventually just dissolve there will  be no more need for a leader or for  elected officials because the people  will take control of all political  decisions and the economic life of the  country directly  and when they do they'll ensure that  there will be no more worker  exploitation no more worker alienation  and certainly no more child labor all  credit and banking will be done by the  state as will all means of communication  and transportation anyone who can work  will they might even do multiple jobs  throughout the day and the profits of  all labor will be shared by everyone in  fact there will be such an abundance  that everyone will have access to what  the labor of the workers produces  everyone will be guaranteed income free  education and free medical care from  each according to his ability to each  according to his need  that's marx's communism  on july 16 1918 several members of the  russian royal family including a father  his wife their five children and  servants were murdered by bolshevik  revolutionaries and dumped into unmarked  graves  the royal family patriarch tsar nicholas  ii had actually been deposed months  before his murder ending 300 years of  romanov family rule  and now revolution was underway across  all segments of society the military  radical leftists and elites many of them  fleeing  what would follow is the creation of a  vast new state known as the soviet union  this was a major experiment that would  test the communist theories of karl marx  as well as endless subsets of this  experiment with such names as the great  industrialization debate nep and their  nadir the star trials of the 1930s in  which brute force prevailed over  collective aims or ideals  so the origins of the soviet union go  back to a time when world war one had  exhausted the russian people and led to  the deaths of millions of russian  peasants conscripted into the tsarist  army  karl marx left no detailed description  of what a real functioning communist  economy would look like  but he assumed that communism would  first triumph in a modern developed  capitalist economy with sophisticated  managers and literate skilled workers  he certainly didn't envision communism  starting in such a poor backward  agricultural and largely illiterate  society as early 20th century russia  consequently vladimir lenin and his  fellow russian bolshevik communists had  to more or less make up the new economic  system on their own when they seized  power  the bolsheviks who constituted the  majority faction of the russian social  democratic party that had seized power  decided on a system of direct control  over the economy  as you probably know mark's theory  wasn't exactly vindicated in the long  run as homer simpson once said  in theory communism works in theory  in reality not so much  what went wrong  well  first  it's well known today that his labor  theory of value is wrong although to be  fair it was the standard theory at the  time smith accepted it as well  much more than the 